spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:12:This specification defines Stage Concurrency Policy for Personal Symphony. The goal is to let a Workspace Repository configure how many agents may run for each Stage Agent while preserving the global `agent.maxConcurrentAgents` cap.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:18:This specification applies to Runtime Settings, scheduler capacity calculation, Ordered Queue admission, dispatch behavior, Runtime State diagnostics, and tests for concurrent Stage Agent execution.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:26:- Increasing concurrency for this Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository before safe parallel Task Branch Integration is implemented.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:32:- **Runtime Settings**: The `settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:33:- **Stage Agent**: A configured stage entry that owns one or more project statuses and transition behavior.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:34:- **Stage Concurrency Policy**: A Runtime Settings rule that limits how many agents may run for a specific Stage Agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:37:- **Task Branch**: A Git branch created from the Loop-Start Branch for one dispatched task.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:38:- **Task Branch Integration**: The act of bringing completed Task Branch commits into the Loop-Start Branch.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:42:- **REQ-001**: Runtime Settings MUST support a Stage Concurrency Policy on each `stageAgents.stages[]` entry.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:43:- **REQ-002**: Stage Concurrency Policy MUST apply to the Stage Agent entry, not to raw project status names.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:44:- **REQ-003**: One Stage Agent that owns multiple statuses MUST share one concurrency limit across all owned statuses.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:46:- **REQ-005**: Symphony MUST NOT exceed either a Stage Agent concurrency limit or the global concurrency cap.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:47:- **REQ-006**: Omitted per-stage concurrency MUST preserve current behavior for that Stage Agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:49:- **REQ-008**: Invalid zero, negative, non-integer, or non-numeric limits MUST be Runtime Settings validation errors.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:52:- **REQ-011**: If one issue is dispatchable for a Stage Agent with limit `2`, Symphony MUST launch only one agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:58:- **CON-001**: This Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository SHOULD keep practical concurrency at one until safe parallel Task Branch Integration is implemented.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:59:- **GUD-001**: After safe parallel Task Branch Integration exists, a recommended dogfood shape is planner `1`, engineer `2`, reviewer `2`, with a global cap high enough to permit the intended total.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:63:### Runtime Settings Shape
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:65:The exact field name may be adjusted during implementation, but per-stage capacity MUST be configured on the Stage Agent entry.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:101:| Stage limit has available slot and global cap has available slot | Dispatch next eligible issue for that Stage Agent. |
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:102:| Stage limit is full | Do not dispatch more issues for that Stage Agent. |
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:104:| Stage has no dispatchable issue | Launch no agent for that Stage Agent. |
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:109:- **AC-001**: Given Backlog limit `1`, engineer limit `2`, reviewer limit `2`, and global cap `5`, When all stages have dispatchable issues, Then Symphony can dispatch up to five agents across those Stage Agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:113:- **AC-005**: Given an Ordered Queue entry is otherwise eligible but its Stage Agent is at capacity, When a later queue entry has different stage capacity, Then queue semantics determine whether the later entry may be admitted.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:120:- **Test Data Management**: Synthetic issue lists, Stage Agent fixtures, Ordered Queue fixtures, and temporary Runtime Settings files.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:138:The policy belongs on Stage Agent entries because a Stage Agent may own multiple project statuses. Limiting raw statuses would split capacity incorrectly and make scheduler behavior harder to reason about.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:140:Safe concurrency also depends on Task Branch Integration. Until unrelated concurrent Task Branches can integrate without avoidable merge attention, this Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository should keep operational concurrency low.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:154:- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Settings and Runtime State.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:195:- A Stage Agent owns `Todo`, `To-Do`, and `In progress`: count all running issues for those statuses against one Stage Agent limit.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:203:- Runtime Settings validation rejects invalid limits.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:212:- [Task Branch Integration specification](./spec-architecture-task-branch-integration.md)
